#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:1
msgid "LinearFitResult"
msgstr "LinearFitResult"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:3
msgid "Definizione"
msgstr "Definition"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:5
msgid ""
"`LinearFitResult` e una `dataclass` immutabile con `slots=True`, usata "
"come oggetto di ritorno di [`lin_fit`](lin-fit.md)."
msgstr ""
"`LinearFitResult` is an immutable `dataclass` with `slots=True`, used as "
"the return object of [`lin_fit`](lin-fit.md)."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:7
msgid "Scopo"
msgstr "Purpose"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:9
msgid ""
"Raccogliere in un unico contenitore tipizzato i parametri del fit, le "
"incertezze associate, i residui, le diagnostiche e la figura opzionale."
msgstr ""
"Collect the fit parameters, associated uncertainties, residuals, "
"diagnostics, and optional figure in a single typed container."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:11
msgid "Campi"
msgstr "Fields"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:13
msgid "`slope`: pendenza della retta stimata."
msgstr "`slope`: slope of the fitted line."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:14
msgid "`intercept`: intercetta della retta stimata."
msgstr "`intercept`: intercept of the fitted line."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:15
msgid "`slope_std`: incertezza standard sulla pendenza."
msgstr "`slope_std`: standard uncertainty on the slope."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:16
msgid "`intercept_std`: incertezza standard sull'intercetta."
msgstr "`intercept_std`: standard uncertainty on the intercept."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:17
msgid "`covariance`: covarianza tra i due parametri del fit."
msgstr "`covariance`: covariance between the two fit parameters."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:18
msgid "`correlation`: coefficiente di correlazione tra pendenza e intercetta."
msgstr "`correlation`: correlation coefficient between slope and intercept."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:19
msgid ""
"`residuals`: vettore dei residui fisici `y - (m x + c)`, sempre non "
"normalizzati anche quando `lin_fit(..., normalize_residuals=True)` mostra"
" residui normalizzati nel grafico."
msgstr ""
"`residuals`: vector of physical residues `y - (m x + c)`, always not "
"normalized even when `lin_fit(..., normalize_residuals=True)` shows "
"normalized residues in the graph."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:20
msgid "`residual_std`: stima sintetica della dispersione dei residui."
msgstr "`residual_std`: compact estimate of residual dispersion."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:21
msgid "`chi2`: chi quadrato del fit."
msgstr "`chi2`: chi-squared of the fit."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:22
msgid "`reduced_chi2`: chi quadrato ridotto."
msgstr "`reduced_chi2`: reduced chi-squared."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:23
msgid ""
"`p_value`: probabilita di ottenere un chi quadrato maggiore o uguale a "
"quello osservato, se il modello e le incertezze sono corretti; vale `nan`"
" con `fit_method=\"residual\"`."
msgstr ""
"`p_value`: probability of obtaining a chi-squared greater than or equal "
"to the observed one, if the model and the uncertainties are correct; it "
"is `nan` with `fit_method=\"residual\"`."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:24
msgid "`dof`: gradi di liberta, pari a `n - 2`."
msgstr "`dof`: degrees of freedom, equal to `n - 2`."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:25
msgid "`iterations`: numero di aggiornamenti dei pesi effettuati."
msgstr "`iterations`: number of weight updates performed."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:26
msgid ""
"`converged`: indica se l'iterazione con `sigma_x` ha soddisfatto il "
"criterio di arresto."
msgstr ""
"`converged`: indicates whether the iteration with `sigma_x` satisfied the"
" stopping criterion."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:27
msgid "`figure`: oggetto matplotlib oppure `None` se `show_plot=False`."
msgstr "`figure`: matplotlib object or `None` when `show_plot=False`."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:28
msgid ""
"`fit_method`: modello di incertezza usato, `\"absolute\"` oppure "
"`\"residual\"`."
msgstr "`fit_method`: uncertainty model used, `\"absolute\"` or `\"residual\"`."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:29
msgid ""
"`scale_factor`: fattore globale applicato alle incertezze con "
"`fit_method=\"residual\"`; vale `1.0` con `fit_method=\"absolute\"`."
msgstr ""
"`scale_factor`: global factor applied to uncertainties with "
"`fit_method=\"residual\"`; `1.0` with `fit_method=\"absolute\"` is valid."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:31
msgid "Quando leggerlo"
msgstr "When to read it"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:33
msgid "Usa questo oggetto quando vuoi:"
msgstr "Use this object when you want to:"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:35
msgid ""
"recuperare i parametri del fit senza dover parsare una stringa o una "
"legenda"
msgstr "retrieve the fit parameters without having to parse a string or a legend"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:36
msgid "controllare la qualita del fit tramite residui, `reduced_chi2` e `p_value`"
msgstr "check fit quality through residuals, `reduced_chi2`, and `p_value`"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:37
msgid "decidere se salvare o riusare la figura generata"
msgstr "decide whether to save or reuse the generated figure"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:39
msgid "Esempio"
msgstr "Example"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:51
msgid "Esportazione in TOML"
msgstr "TOML export"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:53
msgid ""
"Il metodo `to_toml(path)` salva il risultato numerico del fit in un file "
"TOML leggibile e versionabile:"
msgstr ""
"The `to_toml(path)` method saves the numerical result of the fit to a "
"readable, version-controllable TOML file:"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:60
msgid "Il file contiene quattro tabelle:"
msgstr "The file contains four tables:"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:62
msgid ""
"`[mespy]`: `schema_version`, `mespy_version` e `result_type = "
"\"linear_fit\"`, per riconoscere il formato del file."
msgstr ""
"`[mespy]`: `schema_version`, `mespy_version`, and `result_type = "
"\"linear_fit\"`, to identify the file format."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:63
msgid ""
"`[fit]`: `fit_method`, `slope`, `slope_std`, `intercept`, "
"`intercept_std`, `covariance`, `correlation` e `scale_factor`."
msgstr ""
"`[fit]`: `fit_method`, `slope`, `slope_std`, `intercept`, "
"`intercept_std`, `covariance`, `correlation`, and `scale_factor`."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:64
msgid ""
"`[diagnostics]`: `chi2`, `reduced_chi2`, `dof`, `p_value`, "
"`residual_std`, `iterations` e `converged`."
msgstr ""
"`[diagnostics]`: `chi2`, `reduced_chi2`, `dof`, `p_value`, "
"`residual_std`, `iterations`, and `converged`."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:65
msgid "`[residuals]`: il vettore `values` con i residui fisici."
msgstr "`[residuals]`: the `values` vector with the physical residuals."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:67
msgid ""
"Il campo `figure` non viene mai salvato: per conservare il grafico usa il"
" parametro `save_path` di [`lin_fit`](lin-fit.md)."
msgstr ""
"The `figure` field is never saved: to keep the plot, use the `save_path` "
"parameter of [`lin_fit`](lin-fit.md)."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:69
msgid ""
"Se `path` non ha estensione viene aggiunto `.toml`. Un file esistente "
"viene sovrascritto in modo atomico, quindi non resta mai un file a meta. "
"Il metodo restituisce il `Path` del file scritto. I valori vengono "
"salvati con precisione completa: rileggendo il file con `tomllib` si "
"ottengono esattamente gli stessi numeri."
msgstr ""
"If `path` has no extension, `.toml` is appended. An existing file is "
"overwritten atomically, so a half-written file is never left behind. The "
"method returns the `Path` of the written file. Values are saved with full"
" precision: reading the file back with `tomllib` gives exactly the same "
"numbers."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:71
msgid "Note"
msgstr "Notes"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:73
msgid ""
"La classe non esegue calcoli da sola: e una rappresentazione dell'output "
"prodotto da [`lin_fit`](lin-fit.md). Il parametro `normalize_residuals` "
"di `lin_fit` non aggiunge campi e non cambia i valori numerici contenuti "
"in questa classe; agisce solo sul pannello dei residui della figura. Il "
"campo `scale_factor` e invece parte del calcolo: con "
"`fit_method=\"residual\"` descrive la scala di incertezza stimata dai "
"residui."
msgstr ""
"The class does not perform calculations on its own: and a representation "
"of the output produced by [`lin_fit`](lin-fit.md). The "
"`normalize_residuals` parameter of `lin_fit` does not add fields and does"
" not change the numerical values contained in this class; it only acts on"
" the residual panel of the figure. The `scale_factor` field is instead "
"part of the calculation: with `fit_method=\"residual\"` it describes the "
"scale of uncertainty estimated by the residuals."

